# ==============================================================
# OCEAN PUZZLE - INSTRUCTIONS: ROOM 4 (The Ancient Instrument)
# ==============================================================
# Script type : interact
# Bind to     : [FILL IN: x y z of the clickable head block]
# Map/area    : [FILL IN: map name / room]
# Import      : /s i i <paste URL>, then click the head block
#
# What it does:
#   The Oracle explains the instrument in metaphor:
#   - tune each note block ("voice") to the note its symbol
#     ("sign") played in Room 2,
#   - click the Start object to wake the instrument (it only
#     listens for 15 seconds),
#   - play the blocks in order of the Room 3 values, lowest
#     first; straying or retuning mid-song breaks it,
#   - a correct melody raises the parkour path, briefly.
#   Speech lasts about 20 seconds. Can be replayed once every
#   45 seconds per player.
#
# Requires: puzzle1 namespace (see Submit script header)
#
# Related scripts: Instructions Rooms 1-2 and 3 (share the same
#   cooldown), Instrument (10), Finish (11)
# ==============================================================
@using puzzle1
@define Long now = system::currentTimeMillis()

@if oracle_ready_at > now
    @define Long seconds = (oracle_ready_at - now + 999L) / 1000L
    @player &cOracle: You must wait {{seconds}} seconds to hear the instructions again.
    @return
@fi

@var oracle_ready_at = now + 45000L

@player &3Oracle: &bTen voices wait here, each bound to a sign you have already met.
@delay 4s
@player &3Oracle: &bGive each voice the song its sign once sang to you.
@delay 4s
@player &3Oracle: &bThe instrument sleeps. Wake it, and it will listen... but not for long.
@delay 4s
@player &3Oracle: &bThen let the signs speak by their worth: the lightest first, the heaviest last.
@delay 4s
@player &3Oracle: &bHesitate, stray, or shift a voice mid-song, and the melody is lost to the tide.
@delay 4s
@player &3Oracle: &bSing it true, and the deep will open a way onward... though it will not wait for you.
